{"resourceIdentifier":"4413","resourceName":"Household Biogas Program for Smallholder Farmers in India by SPEF and NDDB","description":"The consumption of non renewable biomass firewood for household purposes in the rural areas is one of the main causes of deforestation in the surrou nding areas of the state of Assam, Maharashtra, Jharkhand, Rajasthan, Sikkim and West Bengal and others states of India and has several implications in the environmental and health aspects of such communities. The Project activity aims to replace the commo nly used inefficient wood fired mud stove technology with efficient bio gas based cook stoves, which is clean and sustainable. In view of the same, National Diary Development Board (NDDB), a body corporate constituted an ACT of Parliament called, “The National Diary Development Board Act, 1987” and Sustain Plus Energy Foundation, a Non Profit company incorporated under Section 8 of companies Act 2013, has planned to implement a project which is clean, convenient and efficient energy can be accessed by the rural households.","location":{"latitude":20.593700,"longitude":78.962900},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-06-21","endExclusive":"2023-07-22","endInclusive":"2023-07-21"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4413"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Rajasthan, Sikkim. Uttar Pradesh, West Bengal"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"EKI Energy Services Limited"},{"type":"string","value":"Madhya Pradesh, India"},{"type":"string","value":"919907534900"},{"type":"string","value":"registry@enkingint.org"},{"type":"string","value":"https://enkingint.org/"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"4413"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"